import { s } from './semrush-editorial.js';

export const semrushDepth = {
 1:[
 s('算例：把一项上市目标拆成可验收任务','Worked brief: turn a launch goal into an assignment','假设品牌推出可折叠办公支架，目标用户担心稳定性和收纳。Brief 不写“提高曝光”，而是要求在真实桌面上解释打开、支撑和收起三个环节，同时说明适用限制。\n\n先采购一条解释型内容，再决定是否增加不同场景。到期分别检查约定内容是否完成、观众提出什么问题、访问是否来到对应产品页。若折扣带来订单，也要扣除退款和相关成本。这个模型不预测效果，而是让团队知道下一轮该验证什么。','Consider a hypothetical launch of a folding desk stand. The intended customer worries about stability and storage. Instead of commissioning “awareness,” the brand asks for a demonstration of opening, supporting and packing the stand on an ordinary desk, including relevant limitations. The first purchase is an explanatory assignment with a defined publication window, not an unspecified quantity of exposure.\n\nAfter publication, review three different records. First, did the creator deliver the agreed demonstration? Second, what questions did viewers ask? Third, did recorded visitors reach the matching product page and continue toward the intended action? A missed demonstration is a scope issue; questions about dimensions may indicate a page gap; low relevant distribution suggests a selection or content problem.\n\nIf a discount is involved, account for its effect on contribution as well as tracked orders. Retain refunds and measurement limitations. The example does not predict campaign performance. It shows how a concrete customer uncertainty connects production, analysis and the next decision. The team can then change one part of the system while preserving what was learned from the others.'),
 s('常见问题：多快能判断是否值得继续','FAQ: when is there enough evidence to continue?','先约定观察窗口和需要出现的事件。交付可较早验收；购买路径可能需要更久。窗口内没有足够事件时，结论可以是“暂不足以判断”，而不是硬算一个成功率。\n\n另一问题是是否每个品牌都需要达人营销。若产品事实不清、库存或落地页有明显问题，应先解决这些阻碍。若内容适合解释但没有直接购买入口，可以先把学习目标设为信息理解，并明确尚未验证销售。','Set the review window and the event needed for a decision before the content goes live. Delivery can often be accepted earlier than a purchasing outcome can be evaluated. If the observation window contains too little relevant evidence, “not enough information yet” is a legitimate conclusion. A precise percentage based on almost no events does not make the decision stronger.\n\nA second question is whether every brand needs influencer marketing immediately. If product information is unreliable, stock is unavailable or the destination fails on mobile, solve those constraints before buying more traffic. Creators cannot reliably compensate for an unusable customer experience. If the product needs explanation but an immediate purchase route is unavailable, the first assignment can focus on comprehension or qualified interest, with the untested sales question stated openly.\n\nFinally, ask what would make another batch useful. A repeat should test a specific unresolved hypothesis, extend an evidenced scenario or purchase a clearly needed asset. “We already started” is not a useful renewal criterion. This keeps the program accountable to customer understanding and commercial decisions rather than to a fixed posting habit.'),
 ],
 2:[
 s('算例：同一个产品需要三种不同贡献','Worked example: three contributions to the same product','假设一个家用录音产品要上市。专业解释者可以讲收音限制，生活创作者可以展示家庭使用，UGC 制作者可以拍摄可复用素材。这是三种任务，不是三档影响力高低。\n\n每项任务分别检查作品、范围、受众和许可。没有受众的制作者仍可能适合素材任务；专业人士即使粉丝少，也可能解释得更清楚。品牌不应购买一个称谓，而应采购所需工作。','Imagine a brand launching a home-recording product. A specialist could explain recording limitations, a lifestyle creator could demonstrate an ordinary household situation and a UGC producer could supply reusable advertising assets. These are three contributions, not a ladder of personal importance. The strongest choice depends on which uncertainty the brand needs to resolve.\n\nFor the specialist assignment, review the quality of explanation and whether the proposed statements are supportable. For the lifestyle assignment, inspect comparable scenes and evidence that the audience context fits. For the production assignment, examine asset quality, revisions and permission to reuse the work. A producer without a substantial publishing audience can still be well suited to that third job.\n\nIf one person proposes all three contributions, evaluate them separately in scope and price. Do not infer distribution rights from production ability or technical authority from an engaging personality. The example illustrates why a role-based brief produces a better procurement conversation than “we need an influencer.” The title on an account is a starting description; the relevant work and agreed terms determine whether the assignment is feasible.'),
 s('常见问题：顾客、员工和专家算达人吗','FAQ: can a customer, employee or expert be an influencer?','是否能影响选择与是否适合付费发布，是两个问题。顾客可能拥有真实体验，员工可能有产品知识，专家可能能解释复杂问题，但每种身份都有不同关系与边界。\n\n品牌应记录关系、表达依据与具体使用许可。不要把员工故事包装成独立顾客推荐，也不要把个人经验写成所有用户的结果。一个人能影响小社区，也不代表愿意成为长期品牌大使。','A customer, employee or expert can affect someone’s choices, but influence and suitability for a paid publishing assignment are different questions. A customer may contribute genuine experience, an employee may know the product and an expert may explain a complex issue. Each role brings a different relationship and a different set of boundaries.\n\nRecord the relationship, basis of the statement and permission for the intended use. Do not present an employee story as an independent customer recommendation. Do not turn one person’s experience into an outcome promised to everyone. If a person is comfortable giving private product feedback, that does not establish permission to publish their face, name or quotation in advertising.\n\nA person who influences a small professional community may also have no interest in becoming a recurring brand representative. Ask about the actual assignment rather than treating every useful voice as a prospect for the same program. The role framework helps the brand make these distinctions without requiring a universal definition of who qualifies as an influencer. Capability, relationship, permission and willingness remain separate parts of the decision.'),
 ],
 3:[
 s('算例：给品牌大使写一份角色说明','Worked example: write an ambassador role description','假设跑步配件品牌希望建立六个月社区项目。角色说明可以包含每月一次使用交流、三次主题内容、季度反馈与具体许可期限，但不要求公开任何未经证实的体验。\n\n付费、赠品、活动、独家和退出分别写清。把品牌希望得到的贡献与大使愿意承担的工作对齐；不要用“大使身份”隐去每月工作量和额外出席。','Suppose a running-accessory brand proposes a six-month community program. A useful role description might include a monthly product conversation, three agreed content assignments, a quarterly feedback session and a defined asset license. Those are hypothetical scope choices, not a standard ambassador package. The title itself does not establish any of them.\n\nSeparate paid work, gifts, appearances, exclusivity and exit conditions. State whether a community conversation is private research, a public event or a published asset. Identify what preparation is expected and who coordinates it. A request to attend an additional launch should be treated as a new scope question rather than an invisible duty attached to the ambassador label.\n\nThe creator should be able to describe the role back in ordinary language: what they will do, what they will receive, which statements they can honestly make and how either side handles a change. The brand should be able to connect each obligation to a program objective. If that explanation requires repeated exceptions, simplify the role before recruiting. A smaller, clear commitment is more workable than an impressive title carrying undefined expectations.'),
 s('常见问题：大使必须独家或只收佣金吗','FAQ: must an ambassador be exclusive or commission-only?','独家与佣金都是可谈条款，不是身份自动附带。独家需要明确竞品范围、市场、期限与已有义务；佣金需要订单定义、退款、支付和追踪规则。\n\n项目也需要处理长期使用后的观点变化。允许反馈和诚实表达，设置结束或调整方式，比要求永久正面评价更可执行。续约应依据适配与贡献，而非仅凭称号沿用。','Exclusivity and commission are negotiable terms, not automatic properties of an ambassador role. Define competing categories, markets, duration and existing obligations if exclusivity is required. A broad restriction can prevent unrelated work, so explain the business need and reflect the actual restriction in the commercial discussion.\n\nA commission arrangement needs its own operating definitions: eligible order, refund treatment, tracking route, payment timing and what happens when tracking is unavailable. Commission does not eliminate production effort or guarantee a viable income for the creator. Decide whether a fixed fee, commission or mixed arrangement fits the assignment rather than assuming the title answers the compensation question.\n\nLonger relationships also need a way to handle changing views. Product experience can evolve, and a creator may no longer want to recommend a particular version. Provide a clear review, adjustment and exit process instead of requiring permanent enthusiasm. Renewal should follow evidence of continuing fit, useful contribution and mutual interest. The role can remain valuable while its deliverables change, provided both parties explicitly agree to the new scope.'),
 ],
 4:[
 s('算例：两个相似规模账号的核验路径','Worked example: review two accounts with similar follower totals','假设两个候选都约 30,000 粉丝。甲围绕稳定主题更新，乙最近因抽奖快速增长。先保存作品、增长观察和数据来源，不直接给任何人下造假结论。\n\n品牌需要英国受众时，应请求同口径、带日期的地理证据。若甲提供相关授权报告、乙资料不足，判断是甲的证据更充分，而不是乙必定不真实。把疑点写成下一步问题。','Suppose two candidates each have approximately 30,000 followers. One publishes consistently around the product topic; the other recently ran a giveaway and appears to have grown quickly. Preserve the relevant work, growth observation and source date. Neither pattern alone establishes fraud, purchase intent or commercial suitability.\n\nIf the brand needs a UK audience, request appropriately scoped, dated geography evidence from both candidates. Check whether the report concerns followers, reached accounts or viewers of particular content. Those populations may differ. If one candidate provides relevant authorized evidence and the other cannot, the defensible conclusion is that the first decision is better supported. It is not proof that the second person is dishonest.\n\nWrite unresolved conditions as questions: which audience is represented, what period does the report cover and can the proposed content reach the intended market? Decide whether the remaining uncertainty is acceptable for the project. A small exploratory assignment may tolerate different uncertainty from a large, market-specific purchase. This approach turns an Instagram follower check into a documented risk decision rather than a score used to accuse or automatically approve someone.'),
 s('常见问题：粉丝增长快，是否应该直接拒绝','FAQ: should fast growth trigger an automatic rejection?','快速增长可能有多种原因，公开观察通常不能确认原因。寻找对应作品、报道或活动线索，并请对方解释。解释也需要与时间和数据相符。\n\n同样，低假粉估算不保证内容适合或能卖货。审计只是合作评估的一部分，应与内容、市场、报价、许可和意愿结合。不要为每个人收集与本次决策无关的资料。','Fast growth should trigger a question when it matters to the assignment, not an automatic rejection. Look for a corresponding post, event or other public explanation, and ask the creator when clarification is necessary. The explanation should be consistent with the dates and evidence, but a public observer may still be unable to establish the complete cause.\n\nConversely, a favorable audience-quality estimate does not prove product fit, content quality or sales capability. A technically plausible audience can still be wrong for the market, and an engaging audience can be interested in a topic without intending to buy this product. Keep the audit within its proper role.\n\nCombine audience evidence with comparable content, commercial scope, rights and willingness. Collect only the material needed for the decision, rather than requesting an entire private analytics history from every early lead. The output should explain what was checked, what remains uncertain and why the candidate can or cannot proceed. That record is more useful than a binary “real followers” badge whose definition and date are unavailable to the next reviewer.'),
 ],
 5:[
 s('算例：用同一配件区分不同健身场景','Worked example: one accessory, different training contexts','假设品牌销售便携训练垫。居家力量、旅行拉伸和瑜伽练习都可能相关，但使用问题不同。先选一个场景，验证材质、尺寸和使用限制是否可清楚展示。\n\n候选不是因为贴了健身标签就通过。记录哪条作品体现相同场景、观众问什么，以及产品是否适合实际动作。不要把表现型身材照片当作教学或安全能力证明。','Imagine a brand selling a portable exercise mat. Home strength sessions, travel mobility routines and yoga practice may all be relevant, but they raise different product questions. A home user may care about floor space, a traveler about packing and a yoga practitioner about the intended use conditions. Select one assignment before comparing creators.\n\nA candidate does not pass merely by using a fitness label. Retain a piece of work showing the comparable setting, note the questions viewers ask and confirm that the product is suitable for the planned demonstration. A physique photograph is not evidence of teaching ability, product compatibility or the appropriateness of an exercise for every viewer.\n\nBuild the shortlist around the explanatory task and verify product statements separately. If the brand cannot support a performance claim, changing the creator does not solve the evidence gap. The example helps distinguish the broad “fitness influencers” discovery task from the single-creator pilot guide and the named reference list. Each serves a different decision: mapping suitable contexts, scoping an assignment and studying documented content directions.'),
 s('常见问题：是否只找运动表现最好的人','FAQ: should brands choose only the strongest performer?','运动表现、解释能力和合作能力是不同证据。高水平运动员可能适合竞技叙事，普通生活场景创作者可能更适合解释日常收纳。选择取决于客户问题。\n\n不要要求未经核验的健康结果、减重承诺或观众照做保证。对产品事实与拍摄边界给出清楚资料，创作者也应能表达限制。若关键条件尚未确认，先调整任务。','Sporting performance, explanatory skill and collaboration capability are different forms of evidence. A highly accomplished athlete may be well suited to a competitive story. A creator showing ordinary home routines may be better suited to a storage or convenience question. Neither choice should be made solely from a body type or a follower total.\n\nAsk what the customer needs to understand and which work demonstrates that ability. A product assignment does not require the creator to act as a universal training authority. Avoid unsupported health outcomes, weight-loss promises or assurances that every viewer can reproduce a routine. The brand should supply accurate product information and identify statements that need evidence before the creator develops the story.\n\nIf a key condition remains unresolved, change the assignment or obtain the necessary review before filming. A modest demonstration of setup, dimensions or carrying convenience may be both more useful and more supportable than an ambitious transformation narrative. The collaboration becomes stronger when the limits are visible in the brief rather than added as a hurried caveat after production.'),
 ],
 6:[
 s('算例：从视频线索确认正确 TikTok 账号','Worked example: identify an account from a video clue','假设团队只记得一段厨房短片和近似用户名。先记录可见名称、视频链接、发布时间和主题，再核对官方关联主页，不把搜索第一名当正确身份。\n\n找到相似账号时比较原始发布、内容连续性和其他官方入口。不要仅凭头像或粉丝数合并。确认后保留稳定链接与核验日期，再开展商业联系。','Suppose the team remembers a kitchen video and an approximate username but does not have a reliable profile route. Record the visible name, any surviving video link, approximate publication date and topic. Search from those clues, then compare the candidate with official cross-links or a coherent publishing history. The first result is not automatically the right person.\n\nWhen several similar accounts appear, distinguish an original publisher from a repost or fan account. A matching portrait and a larger follower total are not sufficient reasons to merge identities. Look for consistent original work and appropriate official routes. If the evidence remains ambiguous, keep separate records and state the unresolved identity question.\n\nOnce confirmed, retain the stable profile route and verification date, not only a copied display name that can change. Then check the commercial contact method relevant to the proposed work. This example treats a TikTok user finder as an identity-recovery task. It is deliberately different from searching a broad category for new partners, where several valid candidates may be useful and no single remembered account needs to be recovered.'),
 s('常见问题：找到账号后能否直接外联','FAQ: can you contact the account as soon as it is found?','找到公开主页只解决身份入口，不等于联系方式、可联系意愿或商业条件都已确认。优先使用对方提供的适当商务入口，并说明品牌和相关作品理由。\n\n若账号不可见或无法确认，保留未知，不尝试绕过隐私设置。对更名、删除和跨平台同名都要保留核验记录，避免把旧线索复制成事实。','Finding a public profile establishes an identity route, not necessarily a verified contact, interest in partnership or commercial availability. Prefer the appropriate business route the creator provides. Identify the brand and explain the work-based reason for the message. A personal account discovered through a search does not create an obligation to respond.\n\nIf an account is unavailable or identity cannot be established, preserve the uncertainty. Do not bypass privacy settings to complete a research row. A renamed or deleted account can also make an old search result unreliable, so keep dates and avoid presenting a copied lead as newly checked.\n\nFor names shared across social networks, verify the connection rather than assuming one owner. Conversely, one creator can have several legitimate accounts serving different formats. Decide whether the campaign needs a specific TikTok identity or the broader creator relationship and keep those records connected only when there is evidence. That small distinction prevents duplicate outreach and reduces the chance that a useful search becomes a mistaken commercial conversation.'),
 ],
 7:[
 s('算例：电商品牌如何选择第一条替代路径','Worked example: choose a first alternative route for an ecommerce brief','假设品牌要为一件厨房用品寻找八位能解释使用场景的创作者。先判断需要的是广泛发现、主动报名，还是直接采购明确套餐。三种方式给团队带来的审核工作不同。\n\n把同一任务放入两个适合的入口，记录相关线索、可确认条件和人工工作。不要为了得到赢家而随意更换要求。先选择能完成本轮任务的路径，再谈长期系统。','Suppose an ecommerce brand wants eight research candidates who can explain a kitchen product in an ordinary home. The first choice is not a vendor ranking. It is whether the team needs broad discovery, applications from interested creators or a marketplace route to defined deliverables. Each creates a different review burden and exposes different information.\n\nA discovery route may find a strong content match before commercial interest is known. An application route may reveal interest early while requiring substantial fit review. A packaged offer can clarify a proposed transaction while still leaving audience and usage questions unresolved. Use the same assignment to compare two plausible routes rather than treating their different result counts as equivalent coverage.\n\nRecord relevant leads, available evidence, unresolved commercial conditions and manual work. If the team changes the brief midway, note the change instead of attributing the new result to product superiority. The immediate decision is which route can complete this campaign responsibly. A longer-term system choice can follow after the team understands its repeated workload. This keeps “sites like Tomoson” tied to the job being replaced rather than to a list of superficially similar websites.'),
 s('常见问题：替代网站必须完全复制旧平台吗','FAQ: must an alternative reproduce the old platform exactly?','不必。应保留的是业务任务与必要记录，而不是每个旧按钮。若只做小规模产品体验，复杂付款系统未必必要；若持续运营，记录和权限可能更重要。\n\n不要据旧文章推断 Tomoson 当前状态或价格。核验不足时将其列为未知，不把无法确认升级成停业或安全事件结论。','An alternative does not need to reproduce every old interface element. It needs to support the business task and preserve the records required to perform it. A small product trial may not need a complex payment workflow. A recurring team program may care more about ownership, permissions and continuity than about a large public directory.\n\nSeparate a missing convenience from a missing requirement. A documented manual handoff can be acceptable at low volume, while an unsupported mandatory field may rule out a route entirely. The replacement decision should reflect expected workload and the consequences of an error, not nostalgia for a familiar dashboard.\n\nAlso avoid using old comparison articles to assert Tomoson’s current pricing, availability or operating condition. When a reliable current commercial offering cannot be established, the appropriate state is unresolved. That uncertainty is not evidence of closure, a security incident or any particular cause. Evaluate the documented alternatives on their own terms and confirm current access before committing. A useful comparison can remain honest about an uncertain reference point without inventing a story to make the recommendation sound more complete.'),
 ],
 8:[
 s('算例：一位健身达人的最小可执行 Brief','Worked example: a minimal single-creator fitness brief','假设品牌希望展示训练毛巾的携带与清洁便利。任务是一条在真实训练包场景中的演示，不包含改善运动表现或健康结果的承诺。列出尺寸、材质、清洁说明和不能支持的说法。\n\n样品到达后先确认可用性，再确定拍摄与审核日期。若创作者发现产品不适合场景，应允许在制作前讨论调整，而不是为保证发布压下问题。','Suppose a brand wants to demonstrate how a training towel fits into an ordinary gym bag and how it is cleaned. The assignment is a practical use demonstration, not a claim about improved athletic performance or health outcomes. Supply dimensions, materials, care instructions and any statements the evidence does not support.\n\nDefine one core deliverable, the observation window, the review owner and the intended asset use. Confirm that the sample arrived and is usable before locking the production schedule. A filming date based only on the dispatch date can create avoidable pressure when delivery fails. Keep product fit separate from the creator’s willingness to take the assignment.\n\nIf the creator discovers a real use problem, provide a route to discuss it before production rather than demanding a positive story to preserve the schedule. The team may clarify instructions, revise the assignment or stop the test under the agreed conditions. This is the single-creator pilot’s value: it exposes practical issues before the brand repeats the same brief across a roster. A modest, well-defined test can generate a more useful decision than a larger campaign whose core product demonstration remains unresolved.'),
 s('常见问题：试点是否必须直接带来订单','FAQ: must the pilot produce immediate orders?','是否看订单取决于任务与路径。若任务是解释使用，先看交付和理解证据；若有清晰购买入口，再看访问与有效订单。不要事后把未约定指标设为成败标准。\n\n续约也不只看数字。样品处理、事实准确、反馈效率和许可是否可用，都影响扩量。保留这些记录，下一轮只改变一个主要条件。','Immediate orders are a useful criterion only when the assignment and customer path support that expectation. If the pilot primarily tests whether a use situation can be explained clearly, assess delivery and comprehension evidence first. If there is a working purchase route, review recorded visits and valid orders under the agreed window. Do not introduce an unannounced success criterion after the work is complete.\n\nA zero-order result can have several meanings: insufficient relevant exposure, weak destination fit, a longer buying cycle or incomplete tracking. The small test may not distinguish all of them. Record the uncertainty instead of assigning the entire outcome to the creator.\n\nRenewal also depends on product handling, factual accuracy, communication effort and usable rights. A numerically promising asset can still be difficult to repeat if the agreed license does not support the next use or production required excessive rework. Keep those operational observations with the performance record. For the next test, change one major condition and state why. That makes the pilot a learning instrument rather than a miniature campaign judged by whichever metric looks most favorable afterward.'),
 ],
 9:[
 s('算例：处理拍摄后新增场景的请求','Worked example: handle a new scene requested after filming','假设初始范围是一条厨房使用演示，品牌看到初稿后又希望增加超市场景。负责人先判断是原要求缺失还是新增任务，再让创作者说明成本与时间影响。\n\n记录批准后的新范围、费用、日期和版本。若预算不够，可以保留原交付或减少其他内容，而不是让“修改一轮”无限延长。事前清楚的变更方式能降低合作摩擦。','Suppose the agreed assignment is a kitchen-use demonstration. After reviewing the first cut, the brand asks for an additional supermarket scene. The owner first checks whether the original brief required that location. If it did not, this is a scope-change conversation, not automatically a correction covered by an included revision.\n\nAsk the creator to identify the effect on preparation, filming, permissions, editing and timing. The brand can then accept the additional work, keep the original scope or negotiate a different combination of deliverables. Record the approved fee, date and version in the working record so production does not restart from an ambiguous chat response.\n\nIf the budget cannot support the new scene, a narrower honest choice is better than treating “one revision round” as unlimited new production. Conversely, when an agreed requirement was missed, refer to the existing acceptance criteria and correction process. Both situations can be handled constructively when the distinction is explicit. This worked example shows why clear scope is useful during execution, not merely a formality before payment. The shared record gives both parties a stable basis for deciding what happens next.'),
 s('常见问题：未回复、延迟和拒绝如何处理','FAQ: what should happen after silence, delay or refusal?','未回复可能只是没有兴趣或档期不合。按既定节奏做一次简洁跟进，仍无回应就结束本轮；不要跨多个私人入口追赶。明确拒绝则停止相关邀约。\n\n已确认项目延迟时，先确认阻碍、影响与新日期，区分运输、品牌审批与制作问题。按约定安排修复，不让一个人替所有流程问题承担责任。','Silence can mean lack of interest, timing constraints or simply that the message was not prioritized. Use the team’s bounded follow-up process, keep the reminder concise and close the current invitation if there is no response. Do not pursue the person across unrelated private channels. An explicit refusal should end that proposal unless the creator has clearly invited a different future conversation.\n\nAn active project delay needs a different response. Confirm the obstacle, affected deliverable and revised decision date. Separate shipping problems, slow brand approval and production problems so the corrective action addresses the actual cause. A creator should not silently absorb a deadline lost to a brand’s late feedback, and the brand should not have to guess whether an agreed delivery remains feasible.\n\nRefer to the agreed change, cancellation and payment terms when the scope cannot continue. Retain a concise record of the resolution. Good collaboration does not mean every invitation becomes a project or every project runs without an exception. It means the team handles those exceptions predictably and communicates the next step without turning uncertainty into pressure or blame.'),
 ],
 10:[
 s('算例：从二十份样品开始规划寄送流程','Worked example: plan a twenty-sample seeding batch','假设品牌准备二十份样品，先区分已同意接收、待回复和明确拒绝。只给已确认对象寄送，核对规格、地址用途和可能的配送限制。\n\n状态应分别记为已同意、已寄出、已送达、可选反馈和实际发布。无义务赠送不能把未发布记成未完成交付，也不能把送达数量当成内容数量。','Suppose the team has twenty samples available. Start by separating accepted recipients, unanswered invitations and refusals. Ship only after acceptance, confirming the product variation, appropriate address use and relevant delivery constraints. The sample count is inventory, not an achieved creator partnership count.\n\nUse distinct states for accepted, dispatched, delivered, optional feedback and actual publication. A package arriving does not establish that the creator used it, liked it or promised to post. If the gift is unconditional, absence of a post is not a missed contractual deliverable. A separate agreement is needed when the brand requires content.\n\nThe working file should connect each shipment to a responsible owner and a permitted follow-up route. If the product is lost or arrives unusable, resolve that practical issue before asking for feedback. When comparing alternative sites for this workflow, test whether these distinctions survive exports and team handoffs. The important capability is not merely sending an invitation or generating a shipping label. It is maintaining an accurate relationship record so the brand does not convert a goodwill gesture into an obligation the recipient never accepted.'),
 s('常见问题：样品越多，内容就越多吗','FAQ: do more samples necessarily produce more content?','不会。接受、收到、体验、愿意分享和实际发布是不同事件。没有自己的历史数据时，不设想固定发布比例，更不能将其称为行业保证。\n\n先复盘产品相关性、邀约清晰度与物流，再考虑规模。若品牌需要确定内容，应转为明确的合作采购，并把样品成本与费用分开。','No. Acceptance, delivery, product use, willingness to discuss and actual publication are different events. Without relevant historical evidence from the brand’s own process, do not assume a fixed posting percentage or present it as an industry guarantee. Even an observed past rate depends on the product, recipients, relationship and conditions of that batch.\n\nBefore increasing volume, inspect relevance, invitation clarity and logistics. A larger shipment does not solve an unsuitable product match or a confusing expectation. It can simply multiply cost and create more follow-up work. If the brand needs a definite content commitment, negotiate an explicit collaboration and separate the sample from the production or publication fee.\n\nUse the pilot to decide what kind of program the team actually wants. Unconditional seeding can support product experience and optional feedback, while contracted content purchases deliver a different level of certainty at a different scope. A replacement platform should support that distinction. Selecting a tool that makes everything look like a campaign deliverable can produce misleading reporting even when the packages themselves arrive correctly.'),
 ],
 11:[
 s('怎样把参考名单扩成自己的候选池','Turn a reference list into your own candidate pool','把具名参考的价值拆为内容任务：训练系列、原理解释、动作进阶或瑜伽陪伴。再寻找服务相近任务、市场与规模更适合本次项目的人。\n\n例如需要初学者解释时，记录是否清楚展示选择与限制；需要长期课程场景时，看系列是否连贯。参考名单是研究起点，不等于都应该联系，也不代表知名度排序。','Translate each reference into the content job it illustrates: a training series, technical explanation, movement progression or a yoga-oriented practice context. Then search for other creators serving a comparable job at a market, scale and commercial scope appropriate to the campaign. A famous name can help the team describe a direction without becoming the only viable candidate.\n\nIf the brand needs a beginner-friendly explanation, inspect whether comparable work explains choices and limitations clearly. If it needs a recurring-program setting, examine how a series maintains continuity. Those are observable content questions. They do not establish the audience’s purchasing power or prove that the creator is available.\n\nBuild a small reference board with the specific feature worth studying and the feature that does not transfer. An owned training program, for example, may create a commercial conflict for another program. Use that boundary to find an alternative rather than ignoring it. The resulting candidate pool should be justified by the brand’s assignment, not by resemblance to a celebrity ranking. That is how a “top fitness influencers” article becomes useful research without claiming a universal league table.'),
 s('常见问题：没有当前粉丝排名，名单还有用吗','FAQ: is a shortlist useful without a current follower ranking?','如果用途是研究内容方向，明确身份与作品入口就有价值。但若采购取决于规模、当前受众或档期，就必须补做近期核验。本文不把未知数据伪装成排名。\n\n不同目标也不应共用“最好”标准。教学清楚、娱乐性、制作能力和地域相关都可能重要；先选评价维度，才能决定哪些作品值得比较。','Yes, when its stated purpose is studying content directions. Verified identity routes and documented editorial work can help a team formulate a brief. If the procurement decision depends on current scale, audience composition or availability, those conditions require fresh verification. A reference list should not conceal that missing evidence behind an unsupported rank.\n\nDifferent assignments also need different definitions of “top.” Clear explanation, entertainment, production capability and geographic relevance are distinct dimensions. Decide which matters to the customer problem before comparing work. A creator can be excellent at a role that the current campaign does not need.\n\nWhen you contact a prospective partner, refer to the particular work relevant to the proposed task rather than telling them they occupy a position in a ranking. Request only the additional information needed to evaluate scope. The shortlist is successful when it helps the team recognize a useful direction, understand a limitation and ask a better question. It is not intended to substitute for current commercial diligence or to predict outcomes from the prominence of the names included.'),
 ],
 12:[
 s('算例：先迁移五条记录，再决定整体搬迁','Worked example: migrate five records before moving the whole program','选择五条代表记录：已合作、待回复、有许可、已退出和存在争议的项目。检查身份、状态、合同、素材和历史沟通是否能正确对应。\n\n在新系统核对权限与导出后，由第二位同事复核。若某字段无法迁移，明确保留在哪里与谁负责；不要批量导入后才发现合作状态全部重置。','Choose five representative records before migrating the full program: an active partner, an unanswered invitation, a licensed asset, an ended relationship and a project with an unresolved issue. These expose more useful differences than five identical clean profiles. Match identity, status, agreement, asset route and communication history in the destination.\n\nThen inspect permissions and export the records again. Ask a second teammate to confirm that the current scope and next action are understandable without reading the old system. If a field cannot migrate, document its retained location and owner instead of quietly dropping it. An attachment link that only the original administrator can open is not a complete team handoff.\n\nDo not send messages during the trial import or reset relationship states merely because the destination uses a different label. The point is to preserve meaning, not to make every row look standardized. Once the five-record pilot passes, define the batch process, exception handling and final reconciliation. This approach makes migration reviewable before the team changes a working program, reducing the chance that a new website creates duplicate outreach or loses an existing permission boundary.'),
 s('常见问题：旧数据不完整，要不要全部补齐','FAQ: must every old record be completed before migration?','先判断哪些字段对现有承诺和后续工作必要。已失效的线索与活跃合作可以采用不同处理方式，但都要有可追溯状态。缺失资料标未知，不凭记忆补合同。\n\n迁移完成还需明确旧系统何时停止编辑、谁处理迟到回复，以及取消后的数据访问。旧系统保留不代表大家应继续双向随意更新。','Prioritize fields necessary to honor existing commitments and continue current work. An obsolete research lead does not require the same effort as an active contract or a still-valid asset license. Both need a traceable status, but not every historical blank must be filled before the team can move responsibly.\n\nMark missing material unknown. Do not reconstruct a contract from memory or infer permission from the fact that an asset was used previously. Assign an owner to resolve important gaps and keep the evidence route with the record. The migration should make uncertainty visible rather than laundering an incomplete history into apparently clean data.\n\nAlso define when editing stops in the old system, who handles late replies and what access remains after cancellation. Keeping an archive does not mean everyone should continue updating both systems indefinitely. A clear cutoff and exception process prevents conflicting versions. The migration is complete when active obligations, next actions and evidence locations reconcile, not merely when an import reports a successful row count. That operational definition is more useful than assuming a replacement website automatically inherits the old program’s context.'),
 ],
 13:[
 s('算例：同一粉底产品的三个解释任务','Worked example: three explanatory jobs for one foundation product','假设品牌要展示粉底。色号选择、上妆方法和成分疑问需要不同内容。先明确优先任务，再研究具名参考的表达方法，不要求每个人承担全部角色。\n\n需要实际使用的内容，应确认合适色号、试用时间和可支持说法。不能用灯光或修图替代对真实限制的解释，也不把一次个人体验推广成普遍结果。','Suppose a brand needs content for a foundation product. Shade selection, application technique and ingredient questions are three different explanatory jobs. Decide which uncertainty matters most, then use the named references to study relevant approaches. Do not assume one creator should perform every role or that a recognizable beauty name is suitable for every product.\n\nA use-based assignment needs the right product variation, reasonable trial arrangements and clear boundaries around supportable statements. Agree on how the demonstration will represent the product accurately. A polished image can illustrate technique, but lighting or editing should not replace an honest explanation of limitations. Personal experience should remain personal experience rather than becoming a promised outcome for every viewer.\n\nIf the brand needs several perspectives, explain why each adds something. A technique demonstration and a science-oriented explanation can complement each other; three identical claims may simply repeat the same unsupported proposition. Evaluate the underlying customer job and current comparable work before initiating a commercial conversation. This makes the reference list a tool for planning evidence and content, rather than an assumption that all prominent beauty creators are available interchangeable advertising placements.'),
 s('常见问题：自有美妆品牌是否一定不能合作','FAQ: does an owned beauty brand rule out collaboration?','自有品牌是需要讨论的潜在冲突，不是自动结论。先看具体品类、已有承诺和对方公开政策，再决定是否值得询问。不要推断合作意愿。\n\n品牌也应清楚哪些问题可以让创作者自由评价。赞助不应变成保证好评，专业表达也不能替不充分的产品证据背书。不同市场规则需按实际项目核验。','An owned product line creates a possible conflict, not a universal answer. Check the exact category, known commitments and stated commercial policy before deciding whether an inquiry is sensible. Do not infer willingness from the fact that a creator has collaborated with another brand at some earlier point. A conflict may concern a particular category, market or period.\n\nIf the project proceeds, distinguish factual product information from the creator’s opinion and experience. Sponsorship should not require guaranteed praise. An expert’s presentation style also cannot make unsupported product evidence sufficient. The brand remains responsible for supplying accurate information and resolving claim questions appropriate to the project.\n\nA second issue is whether the reference list establishes current scale. It does not. Current audience evidence, availability, pricing and rights need separate confirmation when they affect the procurement decision. Keep the initial message specific to the relevant work and proposed assignment. A respectful, well-scoped inquiry makes a better next step than asking a creator to confirm a presumed place in a “top” ranking or to endorse a conclusion the brand has already written.'),
 ],
 14:[
 s('算例：诊断一个看似缺少自动化的流程','Worked example: diagnose an apparent automation problem','假设团队每周花两小时寻找最新报价。真正问题可能不是没有自动化，而是回复在不同邮箱、文件命名不一致和无人确认最终范围。\n\n先统一记录所有者与版本，再测试平台是否减少查找和重复工作。若新系统只是增加一处复制粘贴，表面功能更多却未解决交接。用实际净节时与错误记录判断。','Suppose the team spends two hours each week finding the latest quotes. It describes the problem as insufficient automation. Investigation may show that replies are split between inboxes, filenames are inconsistent and no one marks the approved scope. Buying a larger feature set without defining ownership can preserve the same ambiguity in another interface.\n\nFirst establish a record owner and version rule. Then test whether the platform reduces searching, duplicate updates and errors. Follow a quote revision through approval and ask a second teammate to locate the current agreement. Include manual copying and cleanup in the time record. If the new workflow adds another place to paste information, the apparent automation may not create net value.\n\nThis diagnostic does not imply that software is unnecessary. It identifies which handoff the software must support. A product that preserves approved scope and responsibility may be more useful for this team than a sophisticated discovery feature they rarely need. The decision should come from the observed bottleneck and a representative test, with the remaining manual steps written down rather than hidden behind the word “integrated.”'),
 s('常见问题：是否需要一个平台包办全部环节','FAQ: must one platform handle the entire program?','不一定。工具组合可以工作，但交接要有身份、状态与责任规则。若一个系统负责发现、另一个负责合同，必须知道何时以及由谁更新。\n\n端到端系统也要验证实际覆盖范围。越多功能不自动越省事；重要的是完成所需任务的总工作量、证据连续性和退出后的可用记录。','Not necessarily. A combination of tools can work when identity, status and responsibility survive the handoffs. If one system supports discovery and another holds agreements, define when the record moves, who updates it and which system is authoritative for each field. Without that rule, two individually useful tools can create conflicting histories.\n\nAn all-in-one platform also needs verification. Broad coverage in a product description does not establish support for every required market, account type or integration. Ask the team to complete the same real assignment rather than assuming a single login removes all operational work.\n\nCompare the total effort required to maintain a usable record, including training, exception handling and export. The aim is not to maximize the number of tools or minimize it at any cost. It is to make the required work dependable. A platform should earn its place by improving a defined part of the process. When a manual bridge remains acceptable at the current volume, document it and set a review condition instead of adding speculative integrations the team does not yet need.'),
 ],
 15:[
 s('算例：同一内容为什么出现两个互动率','Worked example: why one asset can have two engagement rates','假设内容获得 600 赞和 40 评论，账号有 20,000 粉丝，内容有 10,000 观看。只纳入赞和评论时，分子 640，粉丝口径为 3.2%，观看口径为 6.4%。\n\n两者都可被正确计算，但回答不同问题。不能因为后者更高就宣布表现改善。若添加收藏、分享或更换观察窗口，必须重写口径，不能继续放在同一列比较。','Suppose an asset receives six hundred likes and forty comments. The account has twenty thousand followers, and the asset has ten thousand views. With only likes and comments included, the numerator is 640. Dividing by followers gives 3.2%; dividing by views gives 6.4%. Both calculations can be arithmetically correct while describing different relationships.\n\nThe higher percentage does not show that performance improved. Only the denominator changed. If another report includes saves and shares, its numerator also differs. If it uses the account’s current followers rather than a count captured at publication, timing may differ too. Write those choices into the metric label and retain the underlying values.\n\nFor a comparison, choose one definition and apply it consistently to a relevant group. When a required input is unavailable, show the limitation rather than forcing a percentage into the table. This example is hypothetical and does not represent a platform benchmark. Its purpose is to explain why the first analytical question should be “what was divided by what?” before anyone decides whether a result is high, low or better than another creator’s.'),
 s('常见问题：应该把多条内容的互动率平均吗','FAQ: should you average engagement rates across posts?','逐条比例的平均、合计互动除以合计分母，以及中位数是不同统计。先决定想描述典型内容还是整体量级，再选方法。分母不同的帖子不能随意混算。\n\n例如小流量高比例内容可能拉高简单平均，但对合计结果影响较小。报告保留每条输入、样本选择与窗口，让其他人能复算，而不是只展示最终小数。','A simple average of post-level rates, a ratio of summed interactions to summed denominators and a median are different summaries. Choose the method according to the question. Are you describing a typical post, the combined observed volume or a distribution that contains unusual values? There is no reason to label all three as the same statistic.\n\nA low-volume post with a high percentage can influence a simple average much more than its contribution to a pooled ratio. A median can resist an extreme value while hiding important variation. None of these choices fixes a sample containing incompatible denominators or mixed formats. Review the input group before discussing the summary.\n\nRetain post-level values, the inclusion rule and the observation window so another analyst can reproduce the result. If a creator has too few comparable posts, say so instead of assigning a precise quality score. Engagement rate is a descriptive measure of the chosen inputs, not a complete model of content value, audience honesty or commercial return. That boundary should remain visible when the number is copied into a shortlist or buying presentation.'),
 ],
 16:[
 s('算例：输入前先发现报告中的单位和时间错误','Worked example: audit units and timestamps before entering a report','假设报告把粉丝写成 20K，互动数截图来自周一，观看数来自周五。先将单位恢复为实际计数，再取得相同窗口的数值；不能仅因公式可以计算就接受混合输入。\n\n若缺失的数据无法补齐，使用明确范围的另一种口径或保留未完成状态。让第二人从记录复算，检查其是否得到相同结果。计算器验证的是算术，不是截图真实性、样本代表性或合作价值。','Suppose a report labels followers as 20K, supplies an interaction screenshot from Monday and a view count from Friday. Before typing anything, convert the unit to the actual count and obtain values from a compatible observation window. Entering twenty as though it meant twenty thousand produces a valid arithmetic operation on the wrong scale. Combining unmatched dates can create a different error that the calculator cannot identify.\n\nKeep the original material and transformation notes. If a required value cannot be obtained, use a separately defined measure supported by available evidence or leave the calculation incomplete. Do not fill an unknown component with zero merely to unlock the result. The narrower Instagram worksheet is appropriate when the intended definition explicitly includes only likes and comments.\n\nAsk a second person to reproduce the calculation from the working record without verbal instructions. If their result differs, inspect units, included interactions and denominators before discussing performance. This review tests whether the report is usable, not only whether the interface returns a number. The calculator cannot authenticate screenshots, establish sample representativeness or judge commercial fit. Its value is making the arithmetic transparent once the evidence and definition have been aligned.'),
 s('常见问题：为什么分母为零时不显示百分比','FAQ: why is there no percentage for a zero denominator?','分母为零时，这个比率未定义，不能合理写成零、无穷或默认达标。先检查是内容尚未产生数据，还是字段缺失。空白与零也应区分。\n\n互动总数不一定是独立参与人数。同一个人可以发生多种行为，因此比率也不总能解读为多少人参与。要回答独立用户问题，需要相应数据，不能由此反推。','A zero denominator makes the ratio undefined. It should not be presented as zero engagement, infinite performance or an automatic pass. Check whether the asset has not yet accumulated the relevant observation, whether the field is missing or whether the wrong population was selected. A blank input and an observed zero also mean different things.\n\nAnother common question is whether interactions equal unique participating people. They do not necessarily. One person can perform more than one action, so a sum of likes, comments, saves and shares is an event total under the selected definition. It is not automatically a count of distinct people. A percentage based on that total should not be rewritten as the share of unique users who engaged.\n\nIf the business question needs unique participants, request an appropriate authorized measure and document its scope. Do not reverse-engineer it from an interaction sum. The calculator deliberately keeps arithmetic visible so these questions can be answered before the figure becomes a benchmark or a campaign promise. A useful calculation is one the next reviewer can explain as well as reproduce.'),
 ],
 17:[
 s('算例：一家新店的本地内容安排','Worked example: plan local content for a new venue','假设新加坡一家餐厅希望介绍午餐套餐。先确认地点、营业时间、预订方式、菜单版本和接待能力，再选能解释交通、用餐场景与价格条件的内容。\n\n不要承诺无限接待，也不要让创作者介绍尚未稳定供应的菜。评价和拍摄费用需说清，媒体编辑报道、广告套餐与个人体验是不同关系。','Suppose a Singapore venue wants to introduce a lunch set. Confirm the address, operating hours, booking route, menu version and service capacity before planning content. A useful assignment may need to explain access, dining context and price conditions rather than simply show attractive food. The customer should be able to act on the information without discovering important restrictions after arrival.\n\nDo not create an open-ended invitation when the venue cannot accommodate demand. Confirm the items that can be served during the publication window and identify what happens if a dish changes. A creator should not be asked to describe an unavailable menu from an outdated brief. Keep tasting arrangements, production fees and publication terms explicit.\n\nAn editorial visit, advertising package and personal creator experience are different relationships. Determine which the contact route supports before requesting a favorable article. The publication examples in this guide provide research directions, not a guarantee of availability or a measured local customer base. The strongest local collaboration connects accurate venue information, an appropriate content voice and a feasible customer action, with the commercial relationship understood by everyone involved.'),
 s('常见问题：本地美食账号都覆盖本地顾客吗','FAQ: does a local food account guarantee local customers?','不保证。旅游关注、海外兴趣与本地常客可能同时存在。所在地和题材只能说明相关线索，受众分布与实际到访需要另外核验。\n\n到店、预订与优惠码也不是相同结果。记录取消、重复使用与正常客流背景，不把每次兑换都称为新增顾客。若只验证内容与访问，就明确报告到该阶段。','No. A local food account can attract residents, travelers and overseas viewers interested in the city. Location and topic establish a useful research lead, not a verified customer composition. Request appropriate audience evidence when geography is essential, and keep the source date and population clear.\n\nBookings, visits and code redemptions are also different outcomes. A booking may be canceled; a redemption may come from an existing customer; a visitor may have encountered several other influences. Record the result that is actually observable and avoid calling every code use a newly acquired customer. Consider the venue’s ordinary demand and operational limits when interpreting a publication period.\n\nIf the campaign only establishes content delivery and recorded visits to the menu page, report that stage honestly. A local assignment can still be useful without proving incremental revenue in its first test. The next decision might concern clearer venue information, a different dining occasion or better booking continuity. Use the evidence to improve the customer path rather than assuming a geographically relevant food topic automatically produces profitable footfall.'),
 ],
 18:[
 s('算例：一件高尔夫配件该进入哪种内容','Worked example: place a golf accessory in the right format','假设品牌推出球包收纳配件。它可能适合球场日常、旅行准备或装备整理，不一定需要挥杆教学或性能测试。先确定产品实际解决的问题。\n\n与参考内容比较时，看展示场景、器材与拍摄条件。自营装备品牌和已有赞助可能影响合作，需先询问具体边界，而不是凭题材相近就发通用邀约。','Suppose the product is a golf-bag organizer. It may belong in a course-day routine, travel preparation or equipment-organization story. It does not automatically need swing instruction or a performance test. Start with the actual problem the accessory solves and the scene in which a viewer can understand it.\n\nCompare relevant content formats rather than channel totals. Identify whether the assignment needs course access, travel, equipment or another participant, and confirm the associated scope. A brief for a simple organizer should not quietly acquire the production requirements of a full course feature. Equally, a real equipment test should not be budgeted as a short indoor mention.\n\nOwned product lines and existing sponsorships can affect availability. Ask about the particular category and proposed use rather than assuming a golf creator is commercially available for any golf-related brand. Use the named references to describe a format and find other suitable voices when conflicts exist. This makes discovery more precise: the brand is buying a relevant explanation in a feasible setting, with rights it can use, rather than buying an association with golf as an undifferentiated audience category.'),
 s('常见问题：高尔夫水平能代表内容适配吗','FAQ: does playing ability establish content fit?','竞技能力、教学、娱乐和装备解释是不同贡献。品牌若需要复杂技术表达，要看相近作品；若需要周末出行场景，清晰真实的叙事可能更重要。\n\n不要将个人体验当作所有球手的表现承诺，也不要把观众兴趣推断成购买力。选择依据应能连接产品任务、受众证据与具体制作条件。','Playing ability, instruction, entertainment and equipment explanation are different contributions. A technically demanding assignment needs comparable explanatory work. A weekend-travel story may depend more on clear contextual storytelling. The best fit follows the product task rather than an assumption that the strongest player is the strongest advertising partner.\n\nPersonal experience should not become a guaranteed performance outcome for all golfers. Likewise, an audience’s interest in the sport does not prove budget, location or intent to purchase this product. Verify the conditions that matter to the actual commercial decision and leave the others uncertain.\n\nWhen a proposal is attractive but too broad, narrow it to one supportable demonstration or one customer question. Define what would count as useful evidence after publication: relevant product-page visits, inquiries, an appropriate qualitative response or another agreed stage. Do not change the criterion simply because a particular video generates a large view count. A focused golf collaboration can be evaluated more fairly when the brand separates the creator’s sporting identity, content capability, commercial boundaries and the outcome it is actually trying to observe.'),
 ],
 19:[
 s('算例：在公开输入与授权输入之间保持一致','Worked example: keep public and authorized inputs distinct','假设公开可见 600 赞、40 评论，粉丝为 20,000。公开赞评口径得 3.2%。如果之后取得同窗口的收藏和分享，应另建完整互动口径，不覆盖原字段却继续使用旧标签。\n\n计算器默认只含赞评，避免暗示可公开获取所有互动。给报告保留来源与观察时间；不同内容格式和生命周期也要分开比较。','Suppose the publicly observed inputs are six hundred likes, forty comments and twenty thousand followers. A likes-and-comments follower ratio is 3.2%. If authorized saves and shares later become available for the same observation window, create a separately labeled expanded definition rather than overwriting the original number while retaining its old label.\n\nThis calculator starts with likes and comments so it does not imply that every interaction type is publicly accessible. The view input supplies another denominator, not proof that views are unique people. A report should retain the source route, observation time and format alongside the calculation.\n\nWhen comparing assets, align their lifecycle as well as their formula. A newly published asset and an older post may have had different opportunities to accumulate interactions. Mixing them can make a clean arithmetic comparison look more meaningful than it is. The example is hypothetical; it illustrates a reporting method, not a target Instagram rate. Keep the input definition visible so the same spreadsheet does not gradually combine public observations, private analytics and estimates under one apparently consistent percentage.'),
 s('常见问题：为什么不提供统一合格线','FAQ: why is there no universal pass rate?','没有同口径、相近格式与观察窗口，就不能合理设一条通用线。单一百分比也无法说明购买、内容质量或受众真实性。优先建立本项目可比较的样本。\n\n若只有两三条相近内容，说明样本限制，不给账号打精确等级。计算结果可以支持提问，但最终还需内容、市场、报价与许可证据。','A defensible threshold needs a compatible definition, relevant format and observation window. Without those, a universal pass line can reject a suitable creator or approve an unsuitable one for the wrong reason. A single percentage also cannot establish purchasing behavior, content quality or audience honesty.\n\nBuild a comparison group relevant to the assignment and retain its selection rule. If only a few comparable assets exist, disclose that limitation rather than assigning an elaborate account grade. The result may still support a useful question, such as why a particular topic attracts more discussion, without proving that the creator will deliver a commercially superior campaign.\n\nUse the calculator to clarify evidence before making the broader decision. Combine the rate with relevant work, market evidence, feasible scope and rights. A creator with a modest percentage may explain a difficult product well, while an account with a high percentage may attract attention unrelated to the proposed purchase. This is why the calculator displays arithmetic rather than an automatic “hire” recommendation. The brand remains responsible for connecting a measured interaction pattern to the customer job it is actually commissioning.'),
 ],
 20:[
 s('算例：把一次旅行用品发布拆成三条信息','Worked example: structure a travel-product collaboration','假设品牌的收纳袋需要展示容量、使用便利和购买条件。核心演示只回答实际装入什么；行动提醒指向对应版本；页面说明尺寸、配送与退换安排。\n\n发布前让未参与项目的人在手机上走一遍路径。若找不到同款或优惠条件不清，先修复承接，不把问题留给创作者反复解释。','Suppose a travel-organizer campaign needs to explain capacity, convenience and purchase conditions. The core demonstration shows what actually fits and how it is accessed. The action prompt leads to the matching version. The destination explains dimensions, delivery and relevant return conditions. These messages should complement each other rather than repeat an identical paragraph in every format.\n\nBefore publication, ask someone outside the project to follow the route on a phone. Can they recognize the demonstrated product, choose the correct variation and understand the stated offer? If not, fix the destination before paying to send more visitors. A creator should not have to compensate repeatedly for missing storefront information.\n\nKeep the version and offer period with the campaign record. If stock or conditions change, agree on the update rather than leaving the live content and page in conflict. The example does not assume every viewer sees every asset. It creates a coherent path for those who do proceed. A campaign can then investigate where evidence weakens without treating the creator’s post as the sole cause of every downstream result.'),
 s('常见问题：能否把自然发布直接变成广告','FAQ: can an organic post simply become an ad?','不能只凭已经付款或可以下载就推断许可。核对品牌复用、剪辑、广告投放、期限与市场，以及素材中其他权利和当前账号授权。\n\n如果先做自然测试再决定广告，提前约定可选许可和取得方式，减少事后时间压力。广告效果也应与自然表现分别记录，不混成一个“达人结果”。','Do not infer permission from payment, download access or the fact that an organic post is public. Confirm brand reuse, editing, advertising, duration and markets, together with relevant rights in the material and any current account authorization required for the execution. These conditions belong in the scope, not in an assumption made after the asset performs well.\n\nIf the plan is to test organically before deciding on advertising, discuss an optional license and the process for activating it. That can reduce rushed renegotiation without obliging the creator to grant every possible future use. The option still needs clear terms and an explicit decision.\n\nKeep paid and organic outcomes separate. Additional paid distribution can change the audience and observation conditions, so a blended result may conceal what the original publication achieved. Evaluate the advertising purchase against its own spend and customer path. This distinction helps the brand learn from both activities without attributing all later exposure or orders to a single organic post, and it keeps the commercial discussion aligned with the rights actually purchased.'),
 ],
 21:[
 s('算例：对齐点击记录、订单和退款','Worked example: reconcile visits, purchases and refunds','假设某链接有 400 次已记录访问，后台出现 20 笔对应订单，其中两笔取消、三笔退款。先保存原始订单与状态，再按事先定义报告有效订单和净收入，不直接把 20 当净新增顾客。\n\n优惠码可能被转载，也可能遗漏看过内容后直接购买的人。链接与码分别记录，制定去重规则，不将两个总数直接相加。','Suppose a campaign link has four hundred recorded visits and twenty associated orders appear in the order system. Two orders are canceled and three are refunded. Preserve the original order records and status history, then apply the reporting definition agreed before launch. Do not rename twenty gross associated orders as twenty net new customers.\n\nA discount code can be shared beyond the creator’s audience. A viewer may also purchase later without using the link or code. Keep those routes distinct and define how overlaps are reconciled instead of adding their totals. A transaction identifier helps connect records, but the team still needs a rule for the population and status being reported.\n\nIf revenue is the decision criterion, specify gross versus net revenue and the treatment of discounts, refunds and relevant costs. If customer acquisition is the criterion, establish whether the buyer is new under the brand’s definition. This hypothetical reconciliation does not solve every attribution limitation. It prevents a common reporting error: letting a convenient tracking label silently change an observed event into a stronger commercial claim than the evidence supports.'),
 s('常见问题：没有被追踪的购买该如何处理','FAQ: what should happen to purchases that cannot be tracked?','记录测量缺口，不任意按系数补齐。可以使用自愿来源调查或其他方法补充理解，但要说明样本与偏差，不能把所有品牌增长归给达人。\n\n若需要判断增量，应设计适当对照或实验并评估可行性。归因报告描述分配规则；品牌真正要决定的是，在该证据与成本下是否值得继续投入。','Record the measurement gap rather than applying an arbitrary multiplier to fill it. An optional source survey or another research method may add context, but state its sample and limitations. Do not attribute all growth during the publication period to creators simply because the campaign was active at the same time.\n\nIf the question concerns incremental sales, consider whether an appropriate comparison or experiment is feasible. Attribution reports describe a rule for assigning credit; they do not automatically show what would have happened without the campaign. A small program may not generate enough evidence for a precise causal estimate, and that limitation should remain visible.\n\nThe practical decision is whether the available evidence and full cost justify another scoped test. A team can improve tagging, destination continuity or order reconciliation before increasing spend. It can also decide that a particular content asset is useful while its sales contribution remains uncertain. Keeping those conclusions separate makes the report more useful than forcing a single return figure that combines observed purchases, inferred purchases and unexplained assumptions.'),
 ],
 22:[
 s('算例：一个低价选项为何可能不通过','Worked example: why the cheapest option may fail a requirement','假设两个供应商都能发现候选，但只有一个能导出团队必须保留的记录。若导出是硬条件，另一个不应因为价格低和界面好而在加权总分中获胜。\n\n若可以接受手工桥接，要先量化工作并由负责人明确接受，再调整条件。不能在看到价格后悄悄更改评判规则。','Suppose two vendors both produce relevant discovery candidates, but only one supports an export the team must retain for existing obligations. If that export is mandatory, the other product should not win a weighted score merely because it costs less and looks easier to use. The missing requirement is a gate, not a minor deduction.\n\nThe team may decide that a documented manual bridge is acceptable. If so, estimate the work, identify the owner and explicitly revise the requirement before making the final comparison. Do not quietly relax a condition after seeing an appealing price. Retain the reason so the decision can be reviewed when workload changes.\n\nApply the same discipline to unresolved evidence. A sales presentation saying a capability is planned does not equal a verified current feature. A contract commitment may affect the commercial decision, but it should remain labeled as such. This example shows why the matrix separates requirement status from preference scoring. It protects a simple buying process from becoming a numerical justification for a preferred answer, while still allowing the team to make practical trade-offs with a visible owner and cost.'),
 s('常见问题：评分和试点应该由谁完成','FAQ: who should perform the scoring and pilot?','实际使用者、预算负责人和必要的数据或合同负责人各检查自己的部分。不要只由采购看演示，也不要让单一使用者独自承诺团队所有要求。\n\n试点记录应包含输入、权限、日期和可重复步骤。若两人判断不同，回到具体任务和证据，而不是简单平均意见。最终选择写清剩余风险与接受者。','The people doing the work should test usability and handoffs. The budget owner should review the full cost, and the appropriate data or contract owner should review requirements within their responsibility. A procurement-only demonstration can miss daily operational problems, while a single enthusiastic user may not be able to accept obligations on behalf of the entire team.\n\nKeep the pilot small but reproducible. Record the input brief, account permissions, date, steps and output. A second person should be able to understand what passed without relying on the evaluator’s memory. If reviewers disagree, return to the specific task and evidence rather than averaging impressions into a score that conceals the disagreement.\n\nThe final recommendation should name unresolved conditions, the owner accepting them and the trigger for revisiting the choice. That trigger might be higher volume, a new market or an integration becoming essential. This does not require a large procurement bureaucracy. It requires a concise record that preserves why the product fit the current job and what would make the same choice unsuitable later.'),
 ],
 23:[
 s('算例：一件小家具进入改造内容前要确认什么','Worked example: qualify a small furniture makeover assignment','假设品牌希望展示窄边桌。先确认房间尺寸、配送、组装、表面材料与实际使用限制。创作者有改造能力，不代表任何空间都适合该产品。\n\n拍摄可能依赖安装、其他供应商和房间交付。把品牌控制范围和现场依赖分开列出；若需要后续图片或广告复用，提前确认许可，不等项目结束后再索要。','Suppose a brand wants a narrow side table included in a room makeover. Confirm dimensions, delivery, assembly, materials and relevant use limitations before the project commits to a placement. A creator’s design capability does not establish that every room can accommodate the product or that the available version suits the planned scene.\n\nThe schedule may depend on installation, other suppliers and access to the space. Separate what the brand controls from those external dependencies. A delay elsewhere in the room should not become an unexplained failure attributed to one creator or one shipment. Agree on what can change without undermining the assignment and when a scope review is required.\n\nIf the brand needs still images or later advertising use, discuss that at the beginning. A finished room is not automatically a library of freely reusable brand assets. The relevant rights may involve the creator, property, participants or other material. This example turns a visually attractive home-decor idea into a feasible project, with product fit, timing and usable output established before the team relies on the reveal as a launch commitment.'),
 s('常见问题：能否只按漂亮图片选择家居达人','FAQ: are attractive images enough to select a home creator?','图片能说明审美与制作的一部分，不能说明施工、安装、解释或项目管理能力。核验与本次任务相近的完整作品和实际条件。\n\n家居内容也可能有较长制作周期与常青价值。观看窗口、使用许可和产品持续供应要对齐，避免一段长期传播内容指向已下架版本或过期条件。','Attractive images demonstrate part of an aesthetic and production capability. They do not establish installation, practical explanation or project management. Review complete work comparable to the assignment and confirm the actual production conditions. An excellent styling account may be unsuitable for a project requiring technical assembly, while a capable DIY team may need a different scope and schedule from a simple product photograph.\n\nHome content can also have a long production cycle and remain discoverable after publication. Align the observation window, asset license and product availability with that reality. A long-lived article or video pointing to a discontinued version or expired offer can create avoidable customer confusion.\n\nDecide what the brand needs after the initial reveal: a reusable image, a documented use scenario, qualified visits or another specific result. Confirm the permission and measurement route for that result. This keeps selection grounded in the full assignment rather than in a thumbnail alone. The named references help describe content directions; they do not replace a current check of commercial policy, available space, audience evidence or willingness to include the proposed product.'),
 ],
 24:[
 s('算例：游戏发布与外设发布不是同一 Brief','Worked example: distinguish a game launch from a peripheral launch','游戏发布可能需要让观众理解玩法与适合的人；外设发布可能需要展示兼容、设置与使用体验。即使候选同属游戏频道，相关作品也应分别核验。\n\n提前确认游戏版本、素材、发布限制、硬件与演示环境。若追踪愿望单或安装不可获取，就不承诺相应归因结果，按可验证阶段报告。','A game launch may need viewers to understand the play experience and who it suits. A peripheral launch may need compatibility, setup and use experience. The fact that both involve gaming does not make them the same assignment. Inspect relevant work separately and identify the exact explanatory job the creator is being asked to perform.\n\nConfirm the game build, available materials, publication restrictions and demonstration environment. For hardware, verify the relevant system and supported use. A commercially interesting creator can still be a poor fit for a product that cannot be demonstrated accurately within the available setup. Resolve those conditions before fixing the production date.\n\nIf wishlist, install or purchase data cannot be obtained through an appropriate route, do not promise that the campaign will report it. Use the observable stage and preserve the gap. This hypothetical contrast helps a team avoid a common selection error: finding a familiar gaming name first and retrofitting the product task afterward. A better brief starts with the customer uncertainty and then seeks creators whose actual work provides evidence for that kind of explanation or entertainment.'),
 s('常见问题：订阅者数量能预测视频观看吗','FAQ: can subscriber totals predict a video’s views?','订阅总数不是每条内容的保证触达。题材、形式、发布时间与其他因素都会改变观察结果；没有相近作品数据时，不用固定观看率推算。\n\n还应区分频道、个人和制作团队，核验谁提供交付和许可。具名列表只是身份与方向入口，不代表已完成全部最新作品、受众或商务审计。','Subscriber totals are not guaranteed distribution for a particular upload. Topic, format, timing and other conditions can affect the observed result. Without relevant comparable evidence, do not multiply subscribers by a fixed viewing percentage and present the output as a forecast. Even historical comparable results leave uncertainty.\n\nAsk for the information needed to evaluate the actual assignment and keep its date and scope. A channel-wide average may combine formats unrelated to the proposed work. A small relevant sample can be more informative, provided its limitations are stated and it is not used to claim certainty.\n\nAlso distinguish the channel identity, individual presenter and production team. Confirm who supplies the deliverable and who can grant the intended rights. The named list in this guide supplies official identity routes and research directions, not a complete current library, audience or commercial audit. A useful procurement conversation connects those routes to the present task. It does not assume a well-known gaming channel is a standardized advertising product whose output can be predicted from a subscriber count alone.'),
 ],
 25:[
 s('算例：汽车清洁用品的实际拍摄范围','Worked example: scope an automotive cleaning-product demonstration','假设品牌希望展示一款清洁用品。先确认适用表面、版本、使用说明和不能支持的性能说法；演示不应暗示所有车型或材质都适用。\n\n选择合适环境、拍摄车辆与对比条件，记录是否需要额外地点或设备。把品牌提供的产品信息与创作者实际体验分开，避免用画面效果替代可验证依据。','Suppose a brand wants to demonstrate an automotive cleaning product. Confirm the supported surfaces, version, instructions and boundaries of any performance statement. The demonstration should not imply compatibility with every vehicle or material. A relevant car channel is only the first selection condition; the actual product use still needs to fit the proposed scene.\n\nAgree on the vehicle, setting and comparison conditions, and identify any extra location or equipment cost. Keep brand-supplied factual information distinct from the creator’s observed experience. A dramatic visual difference should not substitute for supportable evidence or conceal conditions that materially affect the result.\n\nDefine what the finished asset needs to explain and what the brand intends to do with it afterward. A product-page clip, a published review and a reusable advertisement can require different scope. This example does not provide a cleaning procedure or make a product-safety claim. It shows the procurement questions that should be answered before production. By resolving compatibility, evidence and usage early, the team reduces the chance of paying for an impressive automotive scene that does not accurately represent the product or cannot be used for the intended campaign.'),
 s('常见问题：是否应要求创作者给出确定结论','FAQ: should a creator be required to reach a predetermined verdict?','品牌可以要求准确事实和约定演示，不能以合作为由保证肯定意见。若必须验证某项性能，先确认合适测试与证据，而不是预写结果。\n\n汽车受众也不自动等于本地购车或维修线索。按实际销售区域、产品兼容与业务路径核验。不要用全球观看量预测某门店的到访。','A brand can require factual accuracy and the agreed demonstration. It should not turn a paid assignment into a requirement for a predetermined favorable verdict. If a performance question must be resolved, establish an appropriate evidence and review process rather than writing the result in advance. The commercial relationship does not make an unsupported conclusion more reliable.\n\nA second question concerns audience geography. An automotive audience is not automatically a pool of local vehicle buyers or workshop customers. Check the actual sales region, product compatibility and customer path. Global video views cannot be converted into local visits by applying an assumed percentage.\n\nA creator may still be valuable for a clearly scoped explanatory asset even when local sales evidence is unavailable. Keep that production value separate from unverified lead generation. The brand can purchase the asset it needs and test distribution through a different route, provided the rights support it. This distinction makes the assignment easier to evaluate and avoids attributing every automotive business outcome to the general popularity of the channel.'),
 ],
 26:[
 s('算例：把受众占比条件写成可复算规则','Worked example: specify an audience-share condition','假设项目需要某成年年龄段受众占比至少 40%。先确认工具提供的分箱是否覆盖目标区间，分母是什么，数据是否估算，以及未知值是否被排除。不能拼接不相容年龄区间。\n\n若工具只有不同分箱，应调整问题或请求合适来源，不能把近似值写成精确满足。保留边界与不确定性，交由项目负责人决定能否接受。','Suppose the project requires at least 40% of a defined adult audience band. First confirm whether the tool’s age bands actually correspond to the requested interval, which population forms the denominator, whether the value is estimated and how unknowns are treated. The percentage is a hypothetical project condition, not a recommended threshold.\n\nDo not combine incompatible age bands or assume that a broad interval proves a narrower one. If the available breakdown differs, revise the question or obtain an appropriate source. A nearby estimate should not become an exact pass simply because the result looks convenient. Record what can be supported and what remains unresolved.\n\nThe same care applies to combined geography and age conditions. Separate marginal percentages do not necessarily establish the joint share of viewers meeting both requirements. Ask what the displayed field actually measures. If the tool cannot answer the combined question, say so and let the campaign owner decide whether that uncertainty is acceptable. A transparent search specification is more useful than an elaborate filter string whose output appears precise but does not correspond to the customer population the brand intended to evaluate.'),
 s('常见问题：零结果是否说明市场没有合适达人','FAQ: do zero results mean no suitable creators exist?','不一定。数据覆盖、关键词、语言、阈值和条件组合都可能限制结果。先逐项检查，再放宽一个条件观察变化。不要静默删去关键要求。\n\n若年龄字段无法可靠使用，可回到场景与内容证据继续研究，但输出要标明尚未验证年龄要求。搜索可以继续，原条件也必须继续保留。','No. Coverage, keywords, language, thresholds and combined logic can all constrain the result pool. Inspect those factors one at a time. A zero-result query is evidence about that query in that dataset, not proof that the entire market lacks suitable creators.\n\nStart from a simpler baseline and reintroduce each condition. Record which change removes candidates and whether it reflects a genuine mismatch or missing coverage. If a requirement is relaxed, preserve the original version and explain the trade-off. Do not silently drop the target market or audience condition and label the new output a complete match.\n\nWhen age evidence cannot be used reliably, content and use-context research may still proceed. Mark the age condition unresolved in the candidate record and decide when it must be verified before a commercial commitment. This lets the team make useful progress without pretending that an unavailable field has been satisfied. A good search workflow supports both discovery and honest uncertainty; it does not need every early result to look fully qualified in order to be valuable.'),
 ],
 27:[
 s('算例：比较两个免费入口的真实输出','Worked example: compare two accessible free routes','假设入口甲返回 50 个账号，其中六个有相关作品；入口乙返回 12 个，其中八个相关。数量更大的入口不一定更省时。记录审阅、去重、补证据和导出的完整时间。\n\n同时比较许可范围与可保留字段。一次成功输出不代表长期额度，试用到期与功能变化应在持续使用前重新确认。','Suppose free route A returns fifty accounts, six of which have relevant work, while route B returns twelve accounts, eight of which are relevant. The larger result count does not automatically make route A more useful. Record the time spent reviewing, deduplicating, finding evidence and producing an output a teammate can use. These figures are hypothetical evaluation examples.\n\nAlso compare what the accessible version permits the team to retain. A result visible on screen may not include a usable export or the fields needed for later review. Do not bypass those restrictions. Decide whether a small permitted manual record is enough for the immediate task or whether the missing capability blocks it.\n\nOne successful output does not establish a permanent allowance. Confirm trial expiry, recurring access and any relevant changes before relying on the route for ongoing work. The evaluation should end with a specific conclusion: useful for a limited research batch, suitable for recurring use under known terms or insufficient for the required output. That conclusion is more informative than declaring one tool the best free option from the number of profiles shown on its first screen.'),
 s('常见问题：何时该停止寻找免费方案','FAQ: when should the search for a free option stop?','当继续寻找的时间超过本次任务可能节省的时间，就应重新评估。免费不是唯一目标，完成相关研究才是。可以缩小任务、接受透明人工步骤，或评估付费。\n\n但付费也不自动解决准确性与覆盖。升级前要求同一任务实测，确认多获得什么和仍缺什么。不要因已经投入很多搜索时间就购买不适合的工具。','Reassess when continued tool hunting consumes more effort than the immediate task is likely to save. Free access is a constraint, not the underlying objective. The objective is completing relevant research. The team can narrow the assignment, accept a transparent manual step or evaluate a paid route if those choices fit the budget.\n\nPayment does not automatically solve accuracy, coverage or workflow quality. Before upgrading, run the same task and identify exactly what becomes available and what remains missing. A paid export of unsuitable profiles is still an unsuitable output. A subscription should not be purchased merely because the team has already spent a long time searching for alternatives.\n\nKeep the decision reversible where practical. Complete a bounded batch, preserve the permitted working record and review the actual effort before committing to a longer workflow. This approach respects a limited budget without turning the free-tool search into an endless project of its own. The right stopping point is the route that supports the next informed campaign decision at an acceptable total cost, with its restrictions stated clearly.'),
 ],
 28:[
 s('算例：六位小账号如何分担三种场景','Worked example: assign six smaller creators to three contexts','假设品牌希望解释便携午餐容器，可围绕办公室、通勤和家庭备餐各选两位，比较场景而非让六人重复一句广告。人数与安排只是试点模型。\n\n给每人相同关键事实与不同表达空间，记录样品、交付、许可和结果。若场景不适合产品，先调整任务，不用更大名单掩盖。','Suppose a brand needs to explain a portable lunch container. A six-person pilot might explore office lunches, commuting and family meal preparation with two creators per context. This is a hypothetical design, not an optimal roster size or a statistically conclusive experiment. The aim is to learn which use situations can be explained usefully.\n\nProvide the same essential product facts while allowing different expressions. Keep samples, deliverables, rights and observation windows explicit. Review whether each asset answered its assigned question before comparing any downstream metric. A scene that does not suit the product should be revised rather than hidden inside a larger roster.\n\nThe team may discover that one context generates useful questions but few immediate visits, while another produces clearer product-page interest. Those observations can guide the next brief, provided the sample limits remain visible. Do not claim that two creators establish the performance of an entire customer segment. The example shows how smaller creators can contribute varied contextual evidence without assuming their follower tier itself causes trust or conversion. The program earns expansion through specific learning and usable work, not through the number of small accounts recruited.'),
 s('常见问题：规模小是否可以省略正式约定','FAQ: can smaller collaborations skip explicit terms?','不能因为账号小就省略范围、费用、许可与披露。简单项目可以用简洁确认，但关键事项仍需双方看懂。FTC 可作为美国项目披露问题的官方入口。\n\n创作者投入的制作与沟通时间不会因粉丝少消失。品牌也应获得清楚交付，避免用“互相支持”替代不对等的未说明任务。','Smaller audience size is not a reason to omit scope, compensation, rights or disclosure planning. A simple assignment can use a concise agreement, but both parties still need to understand the work and obligations. FTC guidance provides an official US disclosure reference. The exact requirements should follow the actual market and relationship.\n\nProduction and communication effort do not disappear because the creator has fewer followers. Equally, the brand should receive the clearly agreed deliverable rather than relying on informal goodwill. “Supporting each other” is not a useful substitute for explaining a commercial request. A gift, paid production and commission arrangement need distinct expectations.\n\nKeep the process proportionate: one clear brief, an appropriate record of agreement, a defined feedback route and a closeout. Do not impose a complex enterprise workflow on a modest task, but do not use simplicity to hide important conditions. The objective is a relationship both sides can perform confidently. A well-run small collaboration can remain lightweight while still protecting honest opinions, usable permissions and a fair understanding of what the brand is buying.', ['semFtc']),
 ],
 29:[
 s('改写练习：把含糊期待改成明确说明','Editing exercise: replace implied expectations with clear wording','原句“期待你下周分享并标记我们”包含日期与发布任务，不能放在无义务礼物卡里。若确实无要求，可改为“无需发布；如有产品问题，请联系”。若确实需要发布，应先另行谈合作。\n\n同样，“希望你喜欢”可以是礼貌祝愿，“请给我们好评”则是另一种请求。检查卡片、外联和后续跟进是否一致，不能只修改其中一处。','Consider the sentence “We cannot wait for you to share this next week and tag us.” It introduces a deadline and a publishing task. It does not belong in an unconditional gift note unless a separate collaboration has already established those requirements. If there is no obligation, replace it with a clear statement such as “No post is required; please contact us if you have product questions.”\n\nIf publication really is required, changing the card alone is insufficient. Discuss and agree on the commercial scope before shipping. Likewise, “we hope you enjoy trying it” can be a courteous wish, while “please give us a positive review” requests a favorable opinion. Check the entire relationship rather than treating one polished sentence as a solution.\n\nReview the invitation, card and follow-up together. They should describe the same arrangement. A card saying “no obligation” is undermined by repeated later demands for a post. This editing exercise helps the brand identify hidden requests before they reach a recipient. It also makes internal reporting clearer, because the team knows whether it is tracking optional product experience or a contracted deliverable.'),
 s('常见问题：便签该写多长，要不要放二维码','FAQ: how long should the note be, and should it include a QR code?','长度以能说清关系、产品与联系为准。说明书和完整 Brief 不必挤进卡片，但可靠入口应清楚。若放二维码，测试目标页面与移动访问，并同时写出可用联系方法。\n\n不要把扫描当同意发布或追踪许可。私人地址和规格信息只用于约定目的；物流记录与内容承诺分开维护。','Length should follow the information needed to explain the relationship, product and contact route. The card does not need to contain the full instructions or campaign agreement. It should make the relevant reliable route easy to find. A short clear note is preferable to a long promotional paragraph that hides whether work is expected.\n\nIf using a QR code, test the destination on a phone and ensure the page remains useful during the product-experience period. Provide a usable contact method as well, so the recipient is not forced to scan merely to ask a question. A scan should not be treated as acceptance of a publishing assignment or as permission for unrelated tracking.\n\nHandle shipping details and product specifications for the agreed purpose, and keep logistics records separate from content commitments. The note is a small part of a larger respectful process. Its success is not measured by how many enthusiastic adjectives it contains, but by whether the recipient understands the package, knows what is optional or agreed and can resolve a problem without guessing whom to contact.'),
 ],
 30:[
 s('算例：把食材品牌 Brief 写成食谱任务','Worked example: turn an ingredient brief into a recipe assignment','假设品牌希望展示一款豆类罐头。先明确目标菜式、份量、产品版本、可支持信息和实际测试安排。食谱开发、摄影、发布与复用是不同范围。\n\n选择有相关作品且接受此类商务合作的人。若参考作者明确不接赞助，应尊重政策，只研究内容结构，不将其列为待催回复的销售线索。','Suppose an ingredient brand wants to feature a canned bean product. Define the intended dish, serving context, product version, supportable information and practical testing arrangements. Recipe development, photography, publication and brand reuse are separate scope questions. A single fee label should not conceal all of them.\n\nLook for comparable work and a compatible commercial policy. A strong recipe publisher may be a useful editorial reference while declining sponsored endorsements. Respect that boundary. Study the content structure without turning the author into a sales lead to pursue repeatedly. Find another suitable partner when the proposed relationship is not accepted.\n\nFor a willing candidate, confirm what happens if the product does not work in the planned recipe. Development can reveal a mismatch, and the agreement should provide a way to revise or stop the assignment rather than require a misleading result. Keep factual product information separate from the creator’s culinary judgment. This example shows why food-blogger collaboration needs more than an attractive finished dish: the recipe process, commercial policy and usable rights must fit the brand’s actual task.'),
 s('常见问题：博客文章与社交帖子应如何比较','FAQ: how should a blog article be compared with a social post?','两者的内容寿命、分发、链接与许可不同，不宜只比较一次观看成本。先确定需要食谱可发现性、制作素材、短期触达还是产品访问，再采购对应任务。\n\n长期文章还需确认产品变化、失效链接和更新责任。品牌获得一次发布不等于拥有全文、图片或永久修改权。原站编辑政策仍然有效。','A blog article and a social post can have different discovery paths, lifecycles, link routes and rights. Comparing only cost per immediate view can miss the job being purchased. Decide whether the brand needs a discoverable recipe, production assets, short-term distribution or qualified product visits, then evaluate the corresponding scope.\n\nA longer-lived article also needs clarity about product changes, broken links and update responsibility. Publication does not give the brand ownership of the full text, images or unlimited revision rights. The publisher’s editorial policy remains relevant after the first launch period. If the brand needs its own reusable recipe asset, purchase that permission explicitly.\n\nKeep the reporting window aligned with the intended use while avoiding a promise that evergreen content will produce traffic indefinitely. A useful review may distinguish initial publication results from later observations. The reference authors in this guide illustrate editorial directions and policies; they are not a current ranking of commercial outcomes. The strongest collaboration combines relevant food work, a willing partner and a scope that can be maintained honestly as the product and content age.'),
 ],
};
